{
	"nodes":[
		{"id":"c32269d32f8bf639","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What was EC2-Classic?**|What was EC2-Classic?]]","x":1920,"y":-1095,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"6cbdc28bf662f367","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is EC2-VPC?**|What is EC2-VPC?]]","x":1920,"y":-900,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"4f915cbc9e9b3a03","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is the default VPC?**|What is the default VPC?]]","x":1920,"y":-705,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"221ce6c2ac471074","type":"text","text":"`EC2-Classic` was the old AWS networking model.  \nIn this model, resources used a shared, flat network.  \nThat means EC2 instances were not running inside your own private VPC.  \nMany AWS customers used the shared AWS network model.  ","x":2320,"y":-1095,"width":500,"height":145},
		{"id":"69eefa845772fae8","type":"text","text":"`EC2-VPC` is the current AWS networking model.  \nIn this model, resources run inside isolated virtual networks.  \nThat virtual network is your VPC.  \nThis is more secure and gives you more control.  ","x":2320,"y":-900,"width":500,"height":135},
		{"id":"edac3fe743575e2f","type":"text","text":"AWS creates a default VPC in each Region.  \nThe default VPC uses this CIDR block:\n```\n172.31.0.0/16\n```\nThe default VPC is useful for learning and quick testing.  \n**Should you use the default VPC for production?**  \n?  \nFor real production systems, it is usually better to create a custom VPC.  \nA custom VPC gives you better control over:\n```\nIP ranges\nSubnets\nRouting\nGateways\nSecurity\nNetwork architecture\n```\n**Important VPC components**  \nThere are four important VPC components:\n```\nSubnet\nRoute table\nInternet Gateway\nNAT Gateway\n```\nThese components help control how traffic moves inside and outside your VPC.  ","x":2320,"y":-705,"width":500,"height":765},
		{"id":"596041e3d4ac68a6","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**Does a VPC belong to one AWS Region?**|Does a VPC belong to one AWS Region?]]","x":1920,"y":885,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"3b11028ee0da5014","type":"text","text":"Yes.  \nA VPC belongs to one AWS Region.  \nFor example, if you create a VPC in the Singapore Region, it exists only in that Region.  \nYou can create multiple VPCs in the same Region.  ","x":2320,"y":885,"width":500,"height":144},
		{"id":"d4eb2c4ba780e793","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What came before Amazon VPC?**|What came before Amazon VPC?]]","x":1920,"y":1073,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"0f6504974117356c","type":"text","text":"Amazon VPC came after Amazon EC2.  \nIn the past, AWS had two networking models:\n```\nEC2-Classic\nEC2-VPC\n```","x":2320,"y":1073,"width":500,"height":195},
		{"id":"1dfb8dd4648190e8","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is Amazon VPC?**|What is Amazon VPC?]]","x":1920,"y":120,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"27eff045af545f1d","type":"text","text":"`Amazon VPC` means `Amazon Virtual Private Cloud`.\nAmazon VPC lets you create your own private, controlled, and secure network inside AWS.  \nNormally, if you run servers in a company data center, you need to design the network yourself.\nFor example:\n```\nIP addresses\nSubnets\nRouting\nGateways\nSecurity\n```\nAmazon VPC gives you the same kind of control, but inside the AWS Cloud.\n**Simple idea**  \nA `VPC` is like your own private network inside AWS.  \nInside that network, you can run resources like:\n```\nEC2 servers\nDatabases\nLoad balancers\nContainers\n```\nYou control how those resources connect to each other and to the internet.  ","x":2320,"y":120,"width":500,"height":675},
		{"id":"1800044c2c2c9b19","type":"text","text":"[[2. Aws/1. Aws fcaj/Explore AWS Services/5. Networking Essentials with Amazon Virtual Private Cloud (VPC)/1. In troduction/6. Checklist/1. Checklist for Amazon VPC#**What is a VPC component?**|What is a VPC component?]]","x":1920,"y":1300,"width":350,"height":80},
		{"id":"bb1ed5353404ad7f","type":"text","text":"A `VPC component` is a networking part inside or attached to a VPC.  \nExamples:\n```\nSubnet\nRoute table\nInternet Gateway\nNAT Gateway\nSecurity group\nNetwork ACL\n```","x":2320,"y":1300,"width":500,"height":315}
	],
